# Ownership of store entries.
#
# The maintainers own the tooling, schema, policy and the generated index.
# Each app author owns their own entry file, so they are requested as a
# reviewer on changes to it. Add a line when you accept a new app:
#
#   /apps/com.example.hello.yaml   @example-user
#
# Keep this file sorted by path.
#
# TODO: replace @<OWNER> with the maintainer handle/team once the GitHub
# repository exists — GitHub silently ignores CODEOWNERS lines naming an
# account that cannot be resolved, so a placeholder here is inert, not broken.

*                     @<OWNER>

/apps/                @<OWNER>
